[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller.
Flick stick: push the right stick {rs} toward where you want to face and the view turns to it; the gyro does the fine aiming.
{start} (Escape) opens the game's menu and backs out of every screen in it. In the menu the d-pad {dpad} moves the cursor and {a} picks.
Hold {lb} for the weapon ring, aiming with the right stick {rs}. {rb} switches to the next weapon and {y} to the previous one. {x} picks the Super Shotgun, {b} the Rocket Launcher and {r3} the Axe.
{a} jumps, and swims up in water. Hold {lt} to run; if the port's Always Run is on, it walks instead. {l3} centres the view.
Quake has no use key, reload or crouch: doors open as you walk into them and buttons by being shot or touched.
Hold {select} (Tab) for the scoreboard.
Quick save is a double tap of {start} (F6), and quick load is a long press of {start} (F9).
These are the port's classic keys, written from memory and not checked in the game. Ironwail and vkQuake only ship with the arrow keys bound for movement, so bind W, A, S and D to forward, left, back and right in Options, Controls, and mouse look to always on. If a button does nothing, compare the Controls screen with the keys here.'''

[profiles.guide.edits]
"stick:Left" = { text = "Move" }
"stick:Right" = { text = "Look" }
"trigger:Right" = { text = "Fire" }
"trigger:Left" = { text = "Run (hold)" }
"button:South" = { text = "Jump" }
"button:East" = { text = "Rocket Launcher" }
"button:West" = { text = "Super Shotgun" }
